<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · disaster</p><h1 class="enc-title">Turnip Winter</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1916">1916</a>–<a href="/years/1917">1917</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Steckrübenwinter</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Turnip Winter was the severe food crisis in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> in the winter of 1916–1917, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, when a failed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/potato">potato</a> harvest and the British naval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naval-blockade">blockade</a> left many civilians depending on turnips, normally used as animal fodder. Hunger, disease and malnutrition killed many people and badly damaged civilian morale and trust in the government.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/turnip-winter.jpg" alt="Turnip Winter" width="273" height="515" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Stadt Erfurt · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kohlr%C3%BCbenkarte_stadt_erfurt_1917.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
